                %br/
            %p Now regarding the concrete proof:
            %p The composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi l
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %mo →
                    %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    a^{-1} \circ l
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathscr{V} \to \mathscr{V}
                    \\,,
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{V}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
              (and hence the sought-after real structure). For that, in turn, it is clearly sufficient that
            #eq:InterchangeOfBiAndSesquilinearForms.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi l
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi l
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a^{-1} \circ l
                    \\,=\,
                    l^{-1} \circ a
                    \\,.
            %p because then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi τ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi l
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi l
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi l
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi.mathscript 𝒱
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau \circ \tau
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big(
                    a^{-1} \circ l
                    \\big)
                    \\circ
                    \\big(
                    a^{-1} \circ l
                    \\big)
                    \\;=\;
                    a^{-1} \circ l
                    \\circ
                    l^{-1} \circ a
                    \\;=\;
                    id_{\mathscr{V}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              We now show that this condition
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InterchangeOfBiAndSesquilinearForms"} (3)
              is equivalent to the assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
